            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0460" n="344" xml:id="pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/924.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé Terres.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Legation’s May 10. Inform Livingston that he is authorized to proceed to
                    Ouanaminthe with the Bishop of Cape Haitien and may employ his good offices with
                    a view to making peace between the Government and leaders of the revolution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
